WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:11.110
President Trump recently ended DACA, the program
protecting nearly 700,000 undocumented immigrants

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.099
whose families brought them to the United
States when they were children.

00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:17.980
The program will be in place for the next
six months, giving Congress time to provide

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:22.699
a legislative solution for these undocumented
immigrants, commonly called Dreamers.

00:00:22.699 --> 00:00:26.859
A study published by the Cato Institute finds
that over the next decade, DACA recipients

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:31.109
will add hundreds of billions of dollars to
the economy, and billions of dollars to the

00:00:31.109 --> 00:00:32.390
federal Treasury.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:34.090
Many hold good paying jobs.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:37.030
They spend money in their communities, supporting
employment themselves.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:41.790
A large share are pursuing higher education,
and will add significant value to the economy

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:44.600
when they finish their undergraduate or graduate
degree.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.750
But more is at stake than economics.

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:50.559
The United States gave the Dreamers security,
relieving them of the fear of a knock on the

00:00:50.559 --> 00:00:55.970
door one day, a life shattered, a forceful
return to a country they do not know.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:59.239
Once given, a great nation doesn’t take
that assurance away.

00:00:59.239 --> 00:01:03.270
A morally serious nation doesn’t extend
the hand of welcome to someone one day and

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:05.250
then shove him out the door the next.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.140
Congress should act to protect 
the Dreamers.

